# AdaptiveSLM Research Project - Executive Summary

## Your Questions Answered

### Q1: How can I get something presentable from this project that I can say "I made this"?

**Answer:** Create three deliverables (2-month timeline):

1. **Interactive Web Demo** (Week 1-2)
   - Live website: `https://your-name.github.io/adaptive-slm-demo`
   - Shows your model adapting to user profiles
   - Side-by-side comparison with baseline
   - Shareable link anyone can test
   - **This is your "look what I built" showcase**

2. **Research Paper** (Week 3-6)
   - 8-page conference paper on PAKD (your novel contribution)
   - Submit to ACL, EMNLP, or NeurIPS workshop
   - Pre-print on arXiv for immediate credibility
   - Citable work with your name

3. **Open Source Project** (Week 7-8)
   - GitHub repository with code, models, docs
   - Can show to potential employers/grad schools
   - Demonstrates both research and engineering skills
   - Community engagement (stars, issues, discussions)

**What you can say:**
> "I developed AdaptiveSLM, a profile-aware small language model that adapts 
> its responses based on user expertise. It runs on devices with <512MB RAM 
> using a novel training technique called Profile-Aware Knowledge Distillation. 
> 
> Try it: [demo link]
> Paper: [arxiv link]
> Code: [github link]"

