### Q2: Do I need to train a model from scratch for this project?

**Answer:** **NO** (not initially)

**Recommended path:**

```
Step 1: Fine-tune existing model with PAKD (2 weeks)
├─ Use Qwen2.5-0.5B (already in your /models folder)
├─ Apply your PAKD technique
└─ Validate that profile adaptation works

Step 2: Evaluate results
├─ If improvement >5% → You have a paper! ✅
└─ If improvement <5% → Consider full training or refine method

Step 3: (Optional) Train from scratch (1-2 months)
├─ Only if needed to strengthen claims
├─ Only if you have time and resources
└─ Your code is already set up for this
```

**Why fine-tuning first?**
- Your contribution is the **training methodology** (PAKD), not the architecture
- 90% faster to results
- Still publishable
- Common practice in ML research

**When to train from scratch:**
- After proving PAKD works via fine-tuning
- If you want architectural novelty claims  
- If you have 2+ extra months
- If targeting top-tier conference (NeurIPS, ICLR)

**Analogy:** You invented a new type of fuel efficiency system for cars. You don't need to build the entire car from scratch to prove it works—you can install it in an existing car first. Once proven, you could design a car optimized for your system.

