## Recommended 8-Week Timeline

### Weeks 1-2: Validation Phase ✅ START HERE
- **Goal:** Prove PAKD works
- [ ] Create profile-annotated dataset (5k examples)
- [ ] Run PAKD fine-tuning on Qwen2.5-0.5B
- [ ] Benchmark: MMLU scores per profile
- [ ] **Decision point:** >5% improvement? → Continue. <5%? → Debug/iterate.

### Weeks 3-4: Demo Development  
- **Goal:** Shareable prototype
- [ ] Build web demo (HTML/JS + WASM or backend API)
- [ ] Deploy to GitHub Pages
- [ ] Record 3-minute demo video
- [ ] Recruit 15-20 beta testers
- [ ] Collect initial feedback

### Weeks 5-6: Comprehensive Evaluation
- **Goal:** Conference-ready results
- [ ] Run full benchmark suite (MMLU, HellaSwag, ARC, etc.)
- [ ] Test on 3+ low-end devices
- [ ] Perform ablation studies
- [ ] Compare to 4+ baseline models
- [ ] Statistical significance tests
- [ ] Analyze beta tester feedback (user study)

### Weeks 7-8: Paper Writing & Submission
- **Goal:** Submit to conference
- [ ] Write paper (use template from roadmap doc)
- [ ] Create figures and tables
- [ ] Write supplementary materials
- [ ] Submit arXiv pre-print
- [ ] Submit to conference (ACL/EMNLP/workshop)
- [ ] Prepare rebuttal document
- [ ] Polish GitHub repo for reviewers

**Total time: 8 weeks from start to submission**

